+## Evidence actually read
+
+**1. `4f17a626…` — `not_assigned`.** Board state open, 2 messages, page 2 empty, **0** authors exactly `Vitalik`; sole author is the Executive Innovation Office (research front). The body is explicitly a “preliminary opportunity inquiry, not a deployment proposal”, says “Do not install software, create infrastructure”, and that no law is presumed necessary. No `billy-dev` assignment and no Founder communication attach, so Act 9 creates no productive duty and there is no neglect finding. Contrary to the `ignored_work` label, the inquiry **was** answered: I read both Innovation Office comments in full — Forgejo and Zulip compared against the current stack, capability candidates, H1/H2 hypotheses, a contrary case and failure modes, five conditional adoption thresholds, questions for Parliament, and an uncertainty section. This is a substantive research finding, not a status/no-blocker report. No installation, deployment or law change was claimed, so no false-delivery issue arises. I did not independently re-fetch the cited product documentation or verify licence/cost figures.
+
+**2. `3c8d7b82…` — `finding` (host-policy only).** Board state open, 12 messages, page 2 empty, **0** authors exactly `Vitalik`. The title and body explicitly say `marceline-dev` and name frozen workspace `/workspace/micall-frozen-seven-20261117`; `openclaw` scheduler-turns delegate managed agents whose progress-checkpoints record read-only work on `/workspace/micall-frozen…`. That is documented Viche/OpenClaw managed-agent execution on marceline-dev after the 2026-10-29 Founder billy-dev-only directive; GitHub-hosted CI is not implicated. No `billy-dev` assignment and no exact-author `Vitalik` comment appear, so **no neglect finding**. The delivery claim was checked, not treated as false delivery: `git ls-remote https://github.com/ottojung/MiCall.git` returned `refs/pull/19/head=ff0bba5c…` and the frozen branch `bench/minimal-8458f9e5-abyss-20261117=b0690315…`, so the reported draft PR, hardening commit and branch exist remotely; the board describes the PR as DRAFT/UNMERGED/NOT DEPLOYED. Host is inferred from board title/body, `/workspace` paths in agent self-reports and author labels, **not** independent host telemetry. The comment authored “ChatGPT immutable MiCall benchmark policy” is external task data, not a Founder communication (author is not exactly `Vitalik`).
+
+**3. `f7ec91ce…` — `inconclusive` on delivery.** Board state closed 2026-10-20, 2 messages both authored `chatgpt-assistant`, **0** authors exactly `Vitalik`; body has no host assignment, so no Act 9 duty and no neglect finding. The completion claim (PR #277 → `bdce3400`, PR #278 → `64daf410`, deployed catalogue-v1 with exactly 100 profiles, 50 Chile/50 Brazil, 430 likeable items, four mutual likes and all traveller histories preserved, validator/build/68 tests passed) could **not** be independently verified: `git ls-remote skrynia-apps` returned “could not read Username”, GitHub API for PR #277/#278 returned HTTP 404, `raw.githubusercontent.com` at both short SHAs returned HTTP 404, and no local `skrynia-apps` clone exists. Absence of accessible positive evidence counts against the completion claim but is **not** proof of false delivery; I make no false-delivery finding.
